  "body": "```js\r\nasync_test(t => {\r\n  const frame = document.createElement(\"iframe\");\r\n  frame.src = \"/common/blank.html\";\r\n  frame.onload = t.step_func(() => {\r\n    console.log(\"load\");\r\n    if(frame.contentWindow.location.pathname !== \"/\")\r\n      frame.src = \"/\";\r\n\r\n    frame.contentWindow.onbeforeunload = t.step_func(() => {\r\n      console.log(\"beforeunload\");\r\n    });\r\n    frame.contentWindow.onunload = t.step_func(() => {\r\n      console.log(\"unload\")\r\n    });\r\n  });\r\n  document.body.appendChild(frame);\r\n});\r\n```\r\nFirefox doesn't dispatch `beforeunload` in this testcase, whereas the other browsers do. What's the desired behavior here?\r\n\r\ncc @bzbarsky @hober ",
